WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.880
- [Ray] Principles for Success:

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.090
An Ultra Mini-Series Adventure

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.873
in 30 minutes and in eight episodes.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.133
Episode three: The Five-Step Process.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.010
We've discussed how important it is

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.510
to reflect carefully
after experiencing pain.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.720
When I did this, I was
usually able to discover

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.980
principles that would
prevent me from repeating

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.950
the same mistakes in the future,

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.270
and I could see that being successful

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.050
simply consisted of five steps.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:34.050
Step one is to know your
goals and run after them.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.350
What is best for you
depends on your nature,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.880
so you need to really understand yourself

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.530
and know what you want to achieve in life.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.010
Step two is to encounter the problems

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.960
that stand in the way of
getting to your goals.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.090
These problems are typically painful.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:52.320
If handled badly, some of
them can lead to your ruin.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.880
But to evolve, you need
to identify those problems

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.740
and not tolerate them.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.630
Step three is to diagnose these problems

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.880
to get at their root causes.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.410
Don't jump too quickly to solutions.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.520
Take a step back and reflect
in order to really distinguish

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.240
the symptoms from the disease.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.490
Step four is to design a plan
to eliminate the problems.

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.740
This is where you will
determine what you need

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.780
to do to get around them.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.050
And step five is to execute those designs,

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.880
pushing yourself to do what's needed

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.830
to progress towards your goal.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.300
A successful life essentially consists

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.080
of doing these five steps
over and over again.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.870
This is your personal evolution,

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.470
and you see this process everywhere.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.450
It's just a law of nature.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.330
Think of any product, any organization,

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.150
or any person you know, and you will see

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.200
that this is true for them.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:52.200
Evolution is simply a process
of either adapting or dying.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.530
Conceptually, it looks just like

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:57.320
the five step process I've described.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.800
As you push through this
often painful process,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.850
you'll naturally ascend to higher

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.240
and higher levels of success.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.220
I've found that when I did it better,

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.890
my struggling never became easier

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.100
because the more capable I became,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.340
the greater the challenges
I would take on.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.490
Because different people are
strong and weak at different

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.240
things, most people can't
do all five steps well.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.940
Not facing this reality
means you could stretch

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.670
further than you should, and
as the heights get greater,

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.593
your falls could also be greater.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.660
Sometimes terrible things
happen to all of us in life.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.130
They can ruin us, or they
can profoundly improve us,

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.550
depending on how we handle them.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.210
Something like this
happened to me in 1982.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:48.340
In episode four, I'll
show you what happened

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.653
and the lessons I learned.

